    "long_instructions": "A thrift store is building a multiple linear regression model. They want to predict the best price for clothing items.\r\n\r\nYour job is to encode three features: the age (in months) of the item, whether it’s stained, and the item’s type.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Read the initial program in `main.py`.\r\n- Encode the `stained` data.\r\n- Add your encoding to the `features` list.\r\n- Run the program to check your work. You should see your encoding as a column in the printed feature matrix.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember that, to implement a binary encoding, you can use conditionals while iterating over rows of data.\r\n\r\n```\r\nvaccinated_encoding = []\r\nfor row in data:\r\n  if row[\"stained\"] == \"yes\":\r\n    # Encode data\r\n  else:\r\n    # Encode data\r\n```",
